00:48:37,720 --> 00:48:39,310
快点，快点，快点，快点。
Faster, faster, faster, faster.

903
00:48:39,360 --> 00:48:40,750
‘接下来的几个小时……’
'For the next few hours...'

904
00:48:40,800 --> 00:48:42,070
刹车，然后全油门。
Brake and full throttle.

905
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:44,110
‘..我在《美国Top Gear》结交的新朋友
'.. my new friend from
American Top Gear

906
00:48:44,160 --> 00:48:46,560
‘给了我一套超棒的教学。’
'gave me some excellent tuition.'

907
00:48:49,080 --> 00:48:51,270
二挡，二挡，刹车。
Second gear, second gear, brake.

908
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:53,430
不，对了方向！
No, wrong way.

909
00:48:53,480 --> 00:48:55,030
刹车，刹车，刹车，刹车，刹车。
Brake, brake, brake, brake, brake.

910
00:48:55,080 --> 00:48:58,480
往那儿，往那儿。刹车，刹车，刹车，刹车，刹车。
That way, that way. Brake,
brake, brake, brake, brake.

911
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:01,310
顺便说一句，抱歉啊。
Sorry about that, by the way.

912
00:49:01,360 --> 00:49:03,300
嘿，别在意，别较真。
Hey, no harm, no foul.

913
00:49:03,960 --> 00:49:05,630
‘然后他抽空解释了
'He then took the time to explain

914
00:49:05,680 --> 00:49:09,230
‘赛车那繁复的细节。
'the considerable
complexities of the racing.'

915
00:49:09,280 --> 00:49:12,350
于是有12辆车，然后分成五个小圈。
So, there's 12 cars, and
then there's five heats.

916
00:49:12,400 --> 00:49:14,830
~ 对啊。 ~ 但每个小圈有四圈。
~ Right.
~ But there's four laps in each heat.

917
00:49:14,880 --> 00:49:16,870
你可不是只开一次，要跑两次。
You won't just drive
once, you go twice.

918
00:49:16,920 --> 00:49:18,830
大概两三次吧。
Like, maybe two or three times.

919
00:49:18,880 --> 00:49:23,710
所以第一名得50分，第二名45分，第三名40分。
So, it's 50 points for the
guy in first, 45 and then 40.

920
00:49:23,760 --> 00:49:26,590
接着还有两场半决赛……
Then there's two semifinals...

921
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:29,390
塔纳说，无论我在热身赛表现如何，我都会进到半决赛。
'Tanner said that, no matter
how I did in the heat,

922
00:49:29,440 --> 00:49:32,030
那我肯定会进入半决赛。
'I'd be in one of the semifinals.

923
00:49:32,080 --> 00:49:34,430
然后他向我解释了“鬼牌圈”。
'Then he explained the joker lap.'

924
00:49:34,480 --> 00:49:37,750
不过每场比赛里，你只能走一次鬼牌圈，
But in every one of these
you do the joker lap once,

925
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:40,470
那是一条很长的外侧弯，
which is the long outside,

926
00:49:40,520 --> 00:49:42,030
第一弯的外侧，
outside of turn one,

927
00:49:42,080 --> 00:49:43,950
进去时还有一点小跳。
with a bit of a jump
on the way in there.

928
00:49:44,000 --> 00:49:47,350
~ 好的，那我每场比赛得走一次鬼牌圈？  
~ 没错。
~ OK, so I have to take the
joker lap once per race?
~ Exactly.

929
00:49:47,400 --> 00:49:50,390
鬼牌圈的坑就在这里——至少慢三秒。
Here's the thing with the jokers
- at least three seconds slower.

930
00:49:50,440 --> 00:49:52,590
理想情况下，你会在合适的时候走鬼牌圈，
Ideally, you would take
the joker lap sometime

931
00:49:52,640 --> 00:49:55,750
比如说被别人逼在后面，需要腾出空间时。
if you're behind somebody and
you need to get free track.

932
00:49:55,800 --> 00:49:57,230
要是忘了怎么办？
And what if you forget?

933
00:49:57,280 --> 00:49:59,470
这就是领航员（spotter）至关重要的原因。
That's why the spotter is critical.

934
00:49:59,520 --> 00:50:00,710
领航员是干嘛的？
What's a spotter?

935
00:50:00,760 --> 00:50:05,030
所以，这栋楼上每辆车都会配一个领航员，
So, on top of this building there'll
be one spotter per car

936
00:50:05,080 --> 00:50:07,590
他会通过无线电、你的耳机跟你联系，
that'll be on the radio,
in your headset,

937
00:50:07,640 --> 00:50:10,070
在你开车的时候随时和你说话，
and they'll be able to talk
to you while you're driving,

938
00:50:10,120 --> 00:50:11,950
告诉你什么时候走鬼牌圈，谁在你后面，
when to take the joker,
who's behind you,

939
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:13,070
你现在排几位，
what position you're in,

940
00:50:13,120 --> 00:50:15,670
提供赛道上你需要的各种信息。
give you information that you
need while you're on the track.

941
00:50:15,720 --> 00:50:18,030
所以说，领航员这活儿真是责任重大。
It's quite a responsible
job, the spotter, then.

942
00:50:18,080 --> 00:50:20,030
~ 对，他们得盯紧点。  
~ 没错。
~ Yeah, they have to pay attention.
~ Yeah.

943
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:22,470
我好像……能再把刚才说的再说一遍吗，
I think I've... Can you just
go through that again,

944
00:50:22,520 --> 00:50:23,630
确认我没有弄错？
to make sure I've got it?

945
00:50:23,680 --> 00:50:26,590
总共12辆车，我们每人要跑五场，每场四圈，
12 cars total, we're all here to
race five times, four laps each,

946
00:50:26,640 --> 00:50:30,240
如果你跑鬼牌圈超过一次，就会被罚30秒……
30-second penalty if you take
the joker more than once...

947
00:50:32,720 --> 00:50:37,150
第二天早上，其他车队都在为比赛日做准备时，
The next morning, as all the other
teams prepared for race day,

948
00:50:37,200 --> 00:50:41,240
我在塔纳的车库里，了解我的车子更多细节。
I was in Tanner's garage getting
to know a bit more about my car.

949
00:50:42,680 --> 00:50:44,430
看看这玩意儿有多大。
Look at the size of this.

950
00:50:44,480 --> 00:50:47,030
显然这根本不是普通的空气滤清器。
That's not a standard
air filter, obviously.

951
00:50:47,080 --> 00:50:50,160
~ 那些都不是标配，这根本不标准……  
~ 可能？
~ None of that is standard,
this isn't standard...
~ May?

952
00:50:51,280 --> 00:50:53,020
~ 早上好。  
~ 早上好。
~ Morning.
~ Morning.

953
00:50:53,880 --> 00:50:55,190
你们来这里干嘛？
What are you doing here?

954
00:50:55,240 --> 00:50:58,710
我们听说你们需要领航员——我们就是你的领航员。
Well, we're told you need spotters,
apparently - we are your spotter.

955
00:50:58,760 --> 00:50:59,950
不，不，不，不。
No, no, no, no.

956
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:02,270
不。领航这活儿真的很重要。
No. Spotting is a genuinely
important job.

957
00:51:02,320 --> 00:51:04,750
要告诉你前面是谁，后面是谁……
You have to say who's in front
of you, who's behind you...

958
00:51:04,800 --> 00:51:06,910
~ 显然没人敢站在你后面。  
~ 真好笑！
~ Well, nobody's behind you, obviously.
~ Funny(!)

959
00:51:06,960 --> 00:51:09,110
什么时候走鬼牌圈——你知道鬼牌圈吗？
When to do the joker lap -
do you know about the joker?

960
00:51:09,160 --> 00:51:11,710
~ 有跳吗？  
~ 有跳。  
~ 那我们再告诉你什么时候跳？
~ Is there a jump?
~ There's a jump.
~ And we tell you when to do that?

961
00:51:11,760 --> 00:51:13,470
~ 嗯，那我到底什么时候来啊？
~ 现在啊！
~ 我也不知道。
~ Yeah, so when do I do it?
~ Now!
~ I don't know.

962
00:51:13,520 --> 00:51:16,110
~ 我该在哪一圈走“joker lap”啊？
~ 我也不知道。
~ 那正是答案啊。
~ Which lap do I do the joker lap on?
~ I don't know.
~ Well, exactly.

963
00:51:16,160 --> 00:51:17,550
~ 一共有几圈？
~ 四圈。
~ How many laps are there?
~ Four.

964
00:51:17,600 --> 00:51:18,710
我说，我能不能直接……？
I mean, can I just...?

965
00:51:18,760 --> 00:51:21,350
我今天早上5:15就起床，赶来这里的。
I got out of bed this morning
at 5:15 to be here.

966
00:51:21,400 --> 00:51:24,110
他昨晚和伦尼·亨利一起住在Ramada旅馆。
He stayed in a Ramada Inn
last night with Lenny Henry.

967
00:51:24,160 --> 00:51:26,270
这就是他有多忘恩负义。
And this is how ungrateful he is.

968
00:51:26,320 --> 00:51:29,350
说真的，我昨天只练了点皮毛，
Seriously, I've done a minimal
amount of practice yesterday,

969
00:51:29,400 --> 00:51:31,110
我可不想让两个布偶帮我。
and I don't want two
Muppets helping me.

970
00:51:31,160 --> 00:51:32,630
抱歉我这么直白，但不行。
I'm sorry to be rude, but no.

971
00:51:32,680 --> 00:51:34,790
James，James！你的门没关好。
James, James! Your door's
not shut properly.

972
00:51:34,840 --> 00:51:37,380
~ 好眼力，好眼力，Hammond。
~ 嗯。
~ Good spot, good spot, Hammond.
~ Yeah.

973
00:51:37,840 --> 00:51:40,790
既然我被Pink和Perky拖住了，
Since I seemed to be stuck
with Pinky and Perky,

974
00:51:40,840 --> 00:51:44,120
我们就去看看第一场比赛里其他车手的表现。
we went to watch some of the
other drivers in the first race.

975
00:51:45,840 --> 00:51:48,710
他们一出发就差不多挤在一起，没错吧？
They don't half start off
close together, don't they?

976
00:51:48,760 --> 00:51:50,550
~ 那里随时可能撞车啊！
~ 嗯。
~ You could crash by there!
~ Yeah.

977
00:51:50,600 --> 00:51:52,200
这镜头就是你。
This'll be you.

978
00:52:12,680 --> 00:52:16,670
‘昨天和Tanner一起，我还以为能上个领奖台呢。
'Yesterday with Tanner, I thought
maybe a podium was a possibility.

979
00:52:16,720 --> 00:52:19,590
‘但现在看真赛车…
'But, now I was watching
the real racing...

980
00:52:20,720 --> 00:52:23,120
‘…我决定把目标调低点。’
'.. I decided to aim a bit lower.'

981
00:52:23,680 --> 00:52:27,110
我想更现实点的个人目标应该是
I think maybe a better
personal ambition would be

982
00:52:27,160 --> 00:52:28,230
别被追上一圈。
not to be lapped.

983
00:52:28,280 --> 00:52:31,150
~ 这事儿常发生吗？
~ 我感觉根本没出现过。
~ Does that happen a lot in this?
~ I don't think it's ever happened.

984
00:52:31,200 --> 00:52:34,700
在Rallycross里不可能被追上一圈，赛只有四圈。
You can't be lapped in Rallycross,
it's only four laps.

985
00:52:36,760 --> 00:52:40,150
所以四圈里，如果他们每圈是50秒，
So, in four laps, if they're
doing a 50-second lap,

986
00:52:40,200 --> 00:52:44,550
而你比他们慢超过12秒，
if you're more than 12 seconds
a lap slower than them,

987
00:52:44,600 --> 00:52:48,030
你就会进《吉尼斯纪录》——第一个
you're in the Guinness Book
of Records as the first person

988
00:52:48,080 --> 00:52:50,420
在Rallycross里被追上一圈的人。
EVER to be lapped in Rallycross.

989
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:56,190
‘想到这里，James排好阵容准备首轮热身，
'On that sobering thought, James
lined up for his first heat,

990
00:52:56,240 --> 00:53:00,240
‘面对比他预想的更强的车手们。’
'which featured drivers of a higher
calibre than he'd been expecting.'

991
00:53:01,800 --> 00:53:04,110
Petter Solberg 是个极其出色的，
Petter Solberg is an extremely good,

992
00:53:04,160 --> 00:53:06,270
前世界拉力赛冠军，
former world champion rally driver,

993
00:53:06,320 --> 00:53:07,990
~ 也是本赛道的世界冠军。
~ 没错。
~ and a world champion at this.
~ Yes.

994
00:53:08,040 --> 00:53:10,390
Timmy Hansen 只有22岁。
Timmy Hansen is 22.

995
00:53:10,440 --> 00:53:14,350
他去年在欧洲Rallycross拿到第三名。
He was third in European
Rallycross last year.

996
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:17,400
~ 还有James May。
~ James May，52岁的钢琴手！
~ And James May.
~ James May, 52-year-old piano player!

997
00:53:18,680 --> 00:53:20,750
对车床也很感兴趣！
Interested in lathes!

998
00:53:20,800 --> 00:53:23,540
‘当车手们准备上赛道时…’
'As the drivers prepared
for the off...'

999
00:53:24,920 --> 00:53:27,190
‘…我们在测试通讯系统。’
'.. we were testing the comms.'

1000
00:53:29,960 --> 00:53:32,960
~ 把他带进状态。
~ 嗯，好，我觉得可以。
~ Put him in the mood.
~ Yeah. Yeah, I'd say that.

1001
00:53:35,600 --> 00:53:38,600
把收音机关小点，你把我的耳朵都炸懵了。
Turn the radio down, you're
blowing my ears out.

1002
00:53:40,560 --> 00:53:42,430
天啊，我到底为什么会答应这个？
Gosh, why did I agree to this?

1003
00:53:42,480 --> 00:53:46,120
我旁边是Petter Solberg，耳朵里还塞满了胡说八道。
I've got Petter Solberg next to me
and a load of drivel in my ears.

1004
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:51,270
~ 哦，这简直刺激得要命。
~ 他要跑了吗？
~ Oh, this is unbelievably exciting.
~ Is he going?

1005
00:53:51,320 --> 00:53:55,320
~ 他要跑了，他要跑了！
~ 天啊，詹姆斯，快开始了。
~ He's going, he's going!
~ Oh, my God. James, it's about to start.

1006
00:53:57,280 --> 00:53:59,590
他们起跑了，起跑了。
They've started, they've started.

1007
00:53:59,640 --> 00:54:02,380
他们起跑了，詹姆斯！
起跑了！
They've started, James!
They've started!

1008
00:54:05,120 --> 00:54:07,590
这里相当泥泞，詹姆斯，真是够泥的。
Quite muddy there, James,
it is quite muddy.

1009
00:54:07,640 --> 00:54:09,040
闭嘴！！
Shut up!!

1010
00:54:12,200 --> 00:54:15,720
詹姆斯？詹姆斯，让你知道，后面那辆车是法国的。
James? James, so that you know,
the car behind you is French.

1011
00:54:17,760 --> 00:54:21,190
~ 那么眼光不错，杰里米。
~ 闭嘴，你们俩！！
~ That was good spotting there, Jeremy.
~ Shut up, you two!!

1012
00:54:21,240 --> 00:54:24,550
“当詹姆斯在后面笨拙地转悠时，
'Whilst James bumbled
around at the back,

1013
00:54:24,600 --> 00:54:27,880
其他四位车手为我们奉献了一场精彩秀。”
'the other four drivers were
giving us a sensational show.'

1014
00:54:49,080 --> 00:54:50,670
哦，出大事了！
Oh, big accident!

1015
00:54:50,720 --> 00:54:52,990
他怎么还能继续冲啊？
But how can he still be going?

1016
00:55:02,440 --> 00:55:05,070
“当其他人进入第四圈，也是最后一圈时，
'As the others entered their
fourth and final lap,

1017
00:55:05,120 --> 00:55:07,190
詹姆斯被追上了。”
'James was being caught.'

1018
00:55:09,200 --> 00:55:12,080
加油！还有刹车！
Gas! And brake!

1019
00:55:13,320 --> 00:55:14,710
打进去。
Turn in.

1020
00:55:14,760 --> 00:55:17,630
把屁股挂到外面，詹姆斯。
把屁股挂到外面。
Hang your arse out, James.
Hang your arse out.

1021
00:55:17,680 --> 00:55:20,030
海鸥，詹姆斯，我看到一只海鸥了。
Seagull, James, I've
spotted a seagull.

1022
00:55:20,080 --> 00:55:21,390
闭嘴！！
Shut up!!

1023
00:55:21,440 --> 00:55:23,510
内线，内线。
Inside line, inside line.

1024
00:55:26,360 --> 00:55:29,100
“令人惊讶的是，他居然逃过去了。”
'Amazingly, though,
he got away with it.'

1025
00:55:30,320 --> 00:55:31,790
是啊！你还没被超车。
Yes! You haven't been lapped.

1026
00:55:31,840 --> 00:55:34,630
哈哈！我没被超！
Ha, ha! I wasn't lapped!

1027
00:55:34,680 --> 00:55:37,790
我倒想看看那另外两个傻瓜怎么做到的！
I'd like to see those other
two Muppets do that!

1028
00:55:37,840 --> 00:55:39,390
希望我们没干扰到他。
I hope we weren't distracting to him.

1029
00:55:39,440 --> 00:55:42,030
不，我倒不这么想，他知道我们在这儿，跟着他。
No, I shouldn't think so, he knows
we're there, we're with him.

1030
00:55:42,080 --> 00:55:44,670
~ 那声音让人放心。
~ 感觉像跟他一起开车比赛，
~ It was reassuring noises.
~ It's like racing in the car with him,

1031
00:55:44,720 --> 00:55:47,870
~ 好像我们三个人都在车里，各自握着方向盘。
~ 正是。
~ it's like we're all three in
the car, all with steering wheels.
~ Exactly.

1032
00:55:47,920 --> 00:55:50,870
“在热身赛获胜的Petter Solberg庆祝完后，
'As the winner of the heat,
Petter Solberg, celebrated,

1033
00:55:50,920 --> 00:55:53,460
我们去看看詹姆斯的成绩。”
'we went to check on James's times.'

1034
00:55:55,240 --> 00:55:59,350
~ 他比Petter Solberg慢了32秒。
~ 嗯。
~ He was 32 seconds off Petter Solberg's time.
~ Yeah.

1035
00:55:59,400 --> 00:56:01,550
每圈慢了八秒。
Eight seconds a lap slower.

1036
00:56:01,600 --> 00:56:05,470
好。我们要给他来一次强有力的团队鼓舞，还是直接支援他？
Right. Should we give him a strong
team talk, or should we support him?

1037
00:56:05,520 --> 00:56:07,350
他只需要学会开得更快……
He just needs to learn
to drive faster...

1038
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:09,070
~ 比其他人快点。
~ 对。
~ Faster than the other people.
~ Yeah.

1039
00:56:09,120 --> 00:56:11,660
嗯，自己比自己快点会更好。
Well, faster than himself would help.

1040
00:56:13,640 --> 00:56:16,920
“我决心在下一轮做得更好。”
'I was determined to do
better in the next heat.'

1041
00:56:21,080 --> 00:56:25,070
不过我的跟踪员比第一次还烂。
'But my spotters were even more
useless than in the first one.'

1042
00:56:25,120 --> 00:56:27,070
今晚你们几点得走？
What time have you got to go tonight?

1043
00:56:27,120 --> 00:56:28,990
呃，我只是想抢个先，赶走堵车。
Uh, well, I just want
to beat the traffic.

1044
00:56:29,040 --> 00:56:31,390
你们走M4的哪段？
Which bit of the M4 do you go down?

1045
00:56:31,440 --> 00:56:33,150
呃，从15号出口下去。
Uh, off, at junction 15.

1046
00:56:33,200 --> 00:56:34,750
那接近M5吧？
That is near the M5, isn't it?

1047
00:56:34,800 --> 00:56:37,310
~ 不不，17是奇彭汉。
~ 那是布里斯托尔。
~ No, no, 17 is Chippenham.
~ It's Bristol.

1048
00:56:37,360 --> 00:56:39,400
闭嘴，你们俩！！
Shut up, you two!!

1049
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:44,540
现在轮到小丑。
Now for the joker.

1050
00:56:45,840 --> 00:56:47,670
肯定是17，奇彭汉。
It's definitely 17, is Chippenham.

1051
00:56:47,720 --> 00:56:50,030
我真不敢相信你居然不知道，你这家伙……
I can't believe you don't
know, you do that...

1052
00:56:50,080 --> 00:56:53,430
是啊，但我不走17，我走15，那是马尔伯勒……
Yeah, but I don't go to 17, I go
to 15, so that's Marlborough...

1053
00:56:53,480 --> 00:56:54,470
闭嘴！！
Shut up!!

1054
00:56:54,520 --> 00:56:56,150
~ ……还有……
~ 哎呀！！
~ ..and...
~ Argh!!

1055
00:56:56,200 --> 00:56:59,070
多亏我的同事们，我硬是把另一场四圈赛跑完了。
'No thanks to my colleagues,
I managed to finish

1056
00:56:59,120 --> 00:57:02,590
而且还没被超一圈。
'another four-lap heat
without being lapped.'

1057
00:57:02,640 --> 00:57:05,430
哈哈！来吧！
Ho-ho! Come on!

1058
00:57:05,480 --> 00:57:06,880
太棒了。
Fantastic.

1059
00:57:07,840 --> 00:57:10,350
但是到半决赛的时候，
'But then it was time
for the semifinal,

1060
00:57:10,400 --> 00:57:13,140
我才意识到自己有更大的麻烦。
'and I realised I had
a bigger problem.'

1061
00:57:14,360 --> 00:57:16,670
~ 半决赛是六圈。
~ 哦哟！
~ The semifinal is six laps.
~ Oh-ho!

1062
00:57:16,720 --> 00:57:17,950
那就再长一半。
So it's half as long again.

1063
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:21,350
我算出来，我的好圈——大概只跑了两圈——
And I've worked out, my good laps
- of which I've done maybe two -

1064
00:57:21,400 --> 00:57:23,470
大约慢了四秒左右。
were sort of four seconds
off the pace.

1065
00:57:23,520 --> 00:57:25,590
但我那几圈稍微失误的
But quite a few of my
slightly cocked up ones

1066
00:57:25,640 --> 00:57:27,790
大概慢了八到九秒。
were sort of eight
to nine seconds off.

1067
00:57:27,840 --> 00:57:29,150
所以，在六圈的比赛里……
So, in a six-lap race...

1068
00:57:29,200 --> 00:57:30,950
~ 六圈赛……
~ 嗯。
~ Six-lap race...
~ Yeah.

1069
00:57:31,000 --> 00:57:32,910
……八秒，算下来是48秒，
.. eight seconds, that's 48 seconds,

1070
00:57:32,960 --> 00:57:35,590
那就是50……就是50秒一圈。
and it's a 50... it's
a 50-second lap.

1071
00:57:35,640 --> 00:57:38,150
~ 哦哟！你有危险啦！
~ 会非常、非常接近。
~ Oh, ho-ho! You're in danger!
~ It'll be very, very close.

1072
00:57:38,200 --> 00:57:41,070
~ 这次会很胶着。
~ 这就是考验。
~ This will be quite close.
~ This is the test.

1073
00:57:42,280 --> 00:57:45,510
脑子里翻腾着这恐怖的算式，
'With this terrifying maths
playing on my mind,

1074
00:57:45,560 --> 00:57:47,990
我踏上了起跑格子。
'I took my place on the grid.'

1075
00:57:48,040 --> 00:57:49,550
给我们争口气，詹姆斯，争口气。
Do us proud, James, do us proud.

1076
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:51,830
别让我们失望。
Don't let us down.

1077
00:57:51,880 --> 00:57:54,830
好啦，开始吧，半决赛，六圈。
Right, here we go,
semifinal, six laps.

1078
00:57:54,880 --> 00:57:57,550
如果你们想下注的话……
So, if you'd like to
place your bets...

1079
00:58:03,400 --> 00:58:06,520
我决定在第一圈就把小丑扫除……
'I decided to get my joker
out of the way on lap one...'

1080
00:58:11,440 --> 00:58:14,880
显然，我那只鹰眼跟踪员立刻发现了这一点。
'.. which, obviously, my
eagle-eyed spotters noticed.'

1081
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:19,990
詹姆斯，你在那圈比领头车慢了整整11秒。
James, you were 11 seconds slower
than the lead car on that lap.

1082
00:58:20,040 --> 00:58:22,270
等等，他使了点小把戏吗？
But, wait, did he do the joker?

1083
00:58:22,320 --> 00:58:24,260
哦，可能是这么回事。
Oh, he might have done.

1084
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:28,910
在前面，塔纳在争夺领头位，
'Up front, Tanner was
fighting for the lead,

1085
00:58:28,960 --> 00:58:31,160
而且比赛相当激烈。
'and the racing was intense.'

1086
00:58:37,680 --> 00:58:39,390
与此同时，稍微后面一点，
'Meanwhile, a bit further back,

1087
00:58:39,440 --> 00:58:42,110
我正设法避开危险。
'I was managing to
stay out of danger.'

1088
00:58:44,440 --> 00:58:47,880
好，冲到第二名，保持动力，保持内线！
Right, down to second, keep the
power, keep the inside line!

1089
00:58:51,560 --> 00:58:54,300
不错，真的不错。
That's not bad, that's
genuinely not bad.

1090
00:59:00,800 --> 00:59:03,310
当詹姆斯还剩两圈时，
'When James still had two laps to go,

1091
00:59:03,360 --> 00:59:06,430
我们意识到他快要被背后捅刀了
'we realised he was about
to be stabbed in the back

1092
00:59:06,480 --> 00:59:08,550
被他新交的‘好基友’背叛。
'by his new best friend.'

1093
00:59:11,720 --> 00:59:14,110
~ 那是塔纳。
~ 那塔纳在他后面吗？
~ That is Tanner.
~ Is that Tanner on his tail?

1094
00:59:14,160 --> 00:59:16,830
詹姆斯，实际上是塔纳在你后面。
James, it's actually
Tanner behind you.

1095
00:59:20,480 --> 00:59:22,550
我要把他挡住！
I've got to hold him off!

1096
00:59:30,120 --> 00:59:34,200
詹姆斯，别让美国版《Top Gear》把英国版给甩了。
James, do not let American
Top Gear lap British Top Gear.

1097
00:59:36,520 --> 00:59:38,460
我说错了！
I'm getting that wrong!

1098
00:59:39,120 --> 00:59:40,520
来啊！
Come on!

1099
00:59:43,040 --> 00:59:44,910
好啊，他就在你身后，詹姆斯！
Well, he's right up
behind you, James!

1100
00:59:44,960 --> 00:59:46,510
把车开宽点！
Make your car wide!

1101
00:59:46,560 --> 00:59:49,100
开得宽得我都不知道该怎么说。
Make it as wide as I don't know what.

1102
00:59:51,440 --> 00:59:53,310
他就在那儿。啊！
He's right there. Argh!

1103
00:59:53,360 --> 00:59:54,390
啊！
Aargh!

1104
00:59:54,440 --> 00:59:56,990
靠内线，贴着内线，走内线！
On the inside, stay on the
inside, go on the inside!

1105
00:59:57,040 --> 00:59:58,440
内线！
Inside!

1106
01:00:01,880 --> 01:00:04,220
~ 哦！
~ 哦，詹姆斯他要……！
~ Oh!
~ Oh, James he's going to...!

1107
01:00:11,600 --> 01:00:13,760
啊！啊！！
Aargh! Aargh!!

1108
01:00:17,240 --> 01:00:18,580
烂摊子。
Rubbish.

1109
01:00:20,160 --> 01:00:21,910
~ 在那儿嘲笑他。
~ 工作室，没错。
~ Let's gloat at him there.
~ Studio, yeah.

1110
01:00:21,960 --> 01:00:24,230
~ 工作室。回到工作室。
~ 回到工作室，
~ Studio. Back to the studio.
~ Back to the studio,

1111
01:00:24,280 --> 01:00:25,870
~ 我们会在那儿嘚瑟。
~ 是的。
~ we'll gloat at him there.
~ Yeah.

1112
01:00:25,920 --> 01:00:29,390
~ 因为我真想回家，
我才不想待在这儿……
Cos I want to get home, frankly,
I don't want to be around...

1113
01:00:29,440 --> 01:00:33,510
所以，他要在这里，成为首位在拉力赛中被超圈的人。
So, he'll go here, first person
ever to be lapped in Rallycross.

1114
01:00:33,560 --> 01:00:36,310
~ 不错啊——名字都要印出来了。
~ 对，正是。
~ Nice, though - name in print.
~ Yeah, exactly.

1115
01:00:36,360 --> 01:00:40,910
总之，我们得说，哪怕他在里面，
Anyway, we have to say,
even with him in it,

1116
01:00:40,960 --> 01:00:42,590
拉力赛真是棒极了。
Rallycross is brilliant.

1117
01:00:42,640 --> 01:00:44,790
观看起来很爽，因为，基本上，
It is fabulous to watch
because, basically,

1118
01:00:44,840 --> 01:00:46,910
从起点线到终点线，
from the start line
to the finish line,

1119
01:00:46,960 --> 01:00:49,190
所有车手都全速狂飙。
all the drivers drive
as fast as they can.

1120
01:00:49,240 --> 01:00:51,870
没错，就是这么回事。根本不用省胎，
Yes, that's it. There's
no conserving their tyres,

1121
01:00:51,920 --> 01:00:53,910
别指望有人管油耗，
there's no looking after
the fuel consumption,

1122
01:00:53,960 --> 01:00:55,910
也没有留着胡子的裁判在……
there are no stewards
with moustaches going,

1123
01:00:55,960 --> 01:00:58,110
“哎呀，你撞到他了，
"Oh, no, you've bumped into him,

1124
01:00:58,160 --> 01:01:00,510
“你得在淘气板凳上呆十秒。”
"you've got to spend ten seconds
on the naughty step."

1125
01:01:00,560 --> 01:01:01,870
我跟你说，一级方程式是——
I tell you what Formula One is -

1126
01:01:01,920 --> 01:01:03,750
一级方程式就像手里有点钱
Formula One is like having some money

1127
01:01:03,800 --> 01:01:07,190
再把它存进ISA，免税增值。
and putting in an ISA so that
it matures in a tax-free way.

1128
01:01:07,240 --> 01:01:10,150
拉力赛就像手里有点钱，直接去酒吧撒欢。
Rallycross is like having some money
and going to the pub with it.

1129
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:13,110
~ 对啊，就一次性全砸在狂欢夜上。
~ 正是。
~ Yeah, just blow it on one
big night out, all at once.
~ Exactly.

1130
01:01:13,160 --> 01:01:14,190
我能说一句吗……？
Can I just say...?

1131
01:01:14,240 --> 01:01:16,230
不，你这么说只会更丢人。
No, you'll make yourself
look more ridiculous.

1132
01:01:16,280 --> 01:01:17,470
你会的，他说得对。
You will, he's right.

1133
01:01:17,520 --> 01:01:19,430
再说，这可是炸弹新闻，时间到，该收场了。
And, on that bombshell,
it is time to end.

1134
01:01:19,480 --> 01:01:21,960
非常感谢收看——晚安！
Thank you so much for
watching - good night!

